@baseUrl = http://localhost:5281
@alertId = 44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444
@operationId = 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
@operatorId = 22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222
@supervisorId = 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333
# Supply valid tokens from the configured issuer, with matching subject/role/operation.
@serviceToken = replace-with-service-token
@operatorToken = replace-with-operator-token
@supervisorToken = replace-with-supervisor-token

### Integration: verify an existing AlertService alert and register its operation
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/feedback-alerts/{{alertId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{serviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "operationId": "{{operationId}}" }

### US26 / TS-20: evaluate an alert (201; duplicate by this reporter -> 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{alertId}}/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "classification": "FALSE_ALARM", "reason": "No fatigue; dust obscured camera", "reportedBy": "{{operatorId}}" }

### Read evaluation history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{alertId}}/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### US27: supervisor review (200; original report remains unchanged)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{alertId}}/feedback/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "classification": "INCONCLUSIVE", "observation": "Insufficient evidence", "reviewedBy": "{{supervisorId}}" }

### US27: paginated queue; remove status to include all three states
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/feedback-alerts?operationId={{operationId}}&from=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&status=PENDING&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### US28 / TS-28: proportions 0..1, one final classification per alert
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/analytics/alert-reliability?operationId={{operationId}}&from=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### Process liveness (not database/upstream readiness)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live
